-- State Pension Regulations 2015 (S.I. 2015/173) -- PART 8 (National Insurance Credits), Chapters 1 and 2: regulations 24 to 28.
-- Source: plain-text rendering of legislation.gov.uk, version 2026-04-06 (uksi-2015-173.txt); not the official text.
--
-- A week is identified by its first day. The figures and tests of the 1975 Regulations and of the Social Security Contributions and
-- Benefits Act 1992 (a week's entitlement under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations; the qualifying earnings factor;
-- whether an election by a married woman is in force) are not among the inputs, so each is a stated input.

§ `Part 8 -- National Insurance Credits`

§§ `Regulation 24: interpretation`

-- Paragraph (1) is definitions only; the terms it borrows (qualifying year, post-commencement qualifying year, working tax credit) are
-- the parent Act's and are used as facts. Paragraph (2): no credit under Chapter 3 for a day, or in respect of an event, before
-- 6 April 2016. A week is placed in the year it begins in (regulation 25(3)), so a week beginning before 6 April 2016 has days
-- before it and is out of Chapter 3 (fork F22).
-- src:319 | (2) Nothing in Chapter 3 is to be construed as entitling any person to be credited with earnings or contributions for any day or in respect of any event occurring before 6th April 2016.
@ref Regulation 24(2) (src:319)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a credit under Chapter 3 may be given for the week` `the first day of the week` MEANS
    Day `the first day of the week` AT LEAST Day `the date the Regulations come into force`

§§ `Regulation 25: general provisions`

-- Paragraph (3): a week that falls partly in one tax year and partly in another falls in the year in which it begins. A tax year
-- runs from 6 April to 5 April, and is named here by the calendar year in which it begins.
-- src:325 | (3) Where under this Part a person is entitled to be credited with earnings or a contribution in respect of a week that falls partly in one tax year and partly in another, that week is to be treated as falling in the year in which it begins and not in the following year.
@ref Regulation 25(3) (src:325)
GIVEN `a calendar day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax year a calendar day falls in` `a calendar day` MEANS
    IF   DATE_MONTH `a calendar day` GREATER THAN 4 OR (DATE_MONTH `a calendar day` EQUALS 4 AND DATE_DAY `a calendar day` AT LEAST 6)
    THEN DATE_YEAR `a calendar day`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `a calendar day` MINUS 1

@ref Regulation 25(3) (src:325)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax year a week falls in` `the first day of the week` MEANS
    `the tax year a calendar day falls in` `the first day of the week`

-- Paragraph (1): Chapter 2 credits a pre-commencement qualifying year (a year before 6 April 2016) and Chapter 3 the others.
-- src:321 | (1) For the purposes of Part 1 of the 2014 Act—
-- src:322 | (a) Chapter 2 makes provision for crediting earnings or contributions in respect of a pre-commencement qualifying year;
-- src:323 | (b) Chapter 3 makes provision for crediting earnings or contributions in respect of a qualifying year or a post-commencement qualifying year.
@ref Regulation 25(1) (src:321-323)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the week falls in a year before 6 April 2016` `the first day of the week` MEANS
    `the tax year a week falls in` `the first day of the week` LESS THAN DATE_YEAR `the date the Regulations come into force`

-- Paragraph (2): only to the extent necessary to make the year a qualifying year. The amount needed is a stated input (the
-- qualifying earnings factor is the parent Act's); a year that is already a qualifying year needs nothing.
-- src:324 | (2) Where under this Part a person would, but for this paragraph, be entitled to be credited with any earnings or contributions for a year, or in respect of any week in a year, that person is only to be credited to the extent necessary to make that year a qualifying year.
@ref Regulation 25(2) (src:324)
GIVEN `the amount the person would be credited with` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount needed to make the year a qualifying year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount the person is credited with` `the amount the person would be credited with` `limited by` `the amount needed to make the year a qualifying year` MEANS
    IF   `the amount needed to make the year a qualifying year` AT MOST 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF   `the amount the person would be credited with` AT MOST `the amount needed to make the year a qualifying year`
         THEN `the amount the person would be credited with`
         ELSE `the amount needed to make the year a qualifying year`

§§ `Regulations 26 and 27: credits for a pre-commencement qualifying year`

-- Regulation 26: the person is credited with what they would have been entitled to under the 1975 Regulations for a Category A
-- retirement pension had the 2014 Act amendment not come into force and the person attained pensionable age on 6 April 2016. That
-- counterfactual entitlement is the stated input; the Chapter limits the credit to a pre-commencement year (regulation 25(1)(a)).
-- src:328 | A person is to be credited with the earnings or contributions to which the person would have been entitled under the 1975 Regulations for the purposes of entitlement to a Category A retirement pension had—
-- src:329 | (a) the amendment made by paragraph 55 of Schedule 12 to the 2014 Act (which limits Category A retirement pensions to people who reach pensionable age before 6th April 2016) not come into force, and
-- src:330 | (b) the person attained pensionable age on 6th April 2016.
@ref Regulation 26 (src:328-330)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
      `the person would have been entitled to the credit under the 1975 Regulations on those assumptions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is credited under regulation 26` `the first day of the week` `given` `the person would have been entitled to the credit under the 1975 Regulations on those assumptions` MEANS
        `the week falls in a year before 6 April 2016` `the first day of the week`
    AND `the person would have been entitled to the credit under the 1975 Regulations on those assumptions`

-- src:332 | A person is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution to which the person would have been entitled under section 23A of the 1992 Act (contributions credits for relevant parents and carers), or regulations made under that section, for the purposes of entitlement to a Category A retirement pension had—
-- src:333 | (a) the amendment made by paragraph 55 of Schedule 12 to the 2014 Act (which limits Category A retirement pensions to people who reach pensionable age before 6th April 2016) not come into force, and
-- src:334 | (b) the person attained pensionable age on 6th April 2016.
@ref Regulation 27 (src:332-334)
GIVEN `the first day of the week` IS A DATE
      `the person would have been entitled to a Class 3 contribution under section 23A of the 1992 Act, or regulations made under it, on those assumptions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is credited under regulation 27` `the first day of the week` `given` `the person would have been entitled to a Class 3 contribution under section 23A of the 1992 Act, or regulations made under it, on those assumptions` MEANS
        `the week falls in a year before 6 April 2016` `the first day of the week`
    AND `the person would have been entitled to a Class 3 contribution under section 23A of the 1992 Act, or regulations made under it, on those assumptions`

§§ `Regulation 28 (and, by the same words, regulation 33): spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty's forces`

-- Paragraphs (2), (4), (5) and (6) of regulation 28 and of regulation 33 are word for word the same, so one rule serves both; it
-- is called from each regulation's own rule (regulation 33 is in spr-part8-credits-post2016). "May only be made in respect of a
-- past period" is read as: the whole week is over before the day the application is received (fork F23).
-- src:337 | (2) The conditions are that the person—
-- src:338 | (a) is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty’s forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation, and
-- src:339 | (b) is accompanying the member of Her Majesty’s forces on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State.
-- src:341 | (4) Paragraph (1) does not apply to—
-- src:342 | (a) a person in respect of a week in which the person is entitled to be credited with earnings under—
-- src:343 | (i) regulation 7A (credits for carer’s allowance or carer support payment),
-- src:344 | (ii) regulation 8A (credits for unemployment),
-- src:345 | (iii) regulation 8B (credits for incapacity for work or limited capability for work), or
-- src:346 | (iv) regulation 9E (credits for certain spouses and civil partners of members of Her Majesty’s forces),
-- src:347 | of the 1975 Regulations; or
-- src:348 | (b) a woman in respect of a week in any part of which an election made by her under regulations under section 19(4) of the 1992 Act (reduced rate election for married women) is in force.
-- src:349 | (5) A person is not entitled to be credited with a Class 3 contribution under paragraph (1) unless an application to be so credited is received by the Secretary of State in accordance with paragraph (6).
-- src:350 | (6) An application under paragraph (5) may only be made in respect of a past period and must—
-- src:351 | (a) be on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in such manner as the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient in the circumstances, and
-- src:352 | (b) include such information as may be specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty’s Revenue and Customs.
@ref Regulation 28(2), 28(4), 28(5), 28(6) (src:337-339); regulation 28(4), 28(5), 28(6) (src:341-352)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the conditions for a forces spouse's credit are met` `the facts` MEANS
        `the facts`'s `the person is a spouse or civil partner of a member of Her Majesty's forces, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State for the purposes of occupying accommodation`
    AND `the facts`'s `the person is accompanying the member on an assignment outside the United Kingdom, or is treated as such by the Secretary of State`
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the person is entitled to be credited with earnings in the week under regulation 7A, 8A, 8B or 9E of the 1975 Regulations`)
    AND (NOT `the facts`'s `the person is a woman with a reduced rate election in force in any part of the week`)
    AND `the application is received after the week is over and is in order` `the facts`
    WHERE
        `the application is received after the week is over and is in order` `the application facts` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the application facts`'s `the date the Secretary of State receives the application`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
            WHEN JUST `the day it is received` THEN
                    (Day (`the application facts`'s `the first day of the week`) PLUS 6) LESS THAN Day `the day it is received`
                AND `the application facts`'s `the application is on a form approved by the Secretary of State, or made in a manner the Secretary of State accepts as sufficient in the circumstances`
                AND `the application facts`'s `the application includes the information specified by the Secretary of State or the Commissioners for Her Majesty's Revenue and Customs`

-- src:336 | (1) Subject to paragraph (5), a person who satisfies the conditions in paragraph (2) for any part of a week to which this regulation applies is to be credited with a Class 3 contribution in respect of that week.
-- src:340 | (3) This regulation applies to a week which falls within a year beginning on or after 6th April 1975 and ending before 6th April 2016 for which the earnings factors of the member of Her Majesty’s forces exceed the qualifying earnings factor.
@ref Regulation 28(1), 28(3) (src:336); regulation 28(3) (src:340)
GIVEN `the facts` IS A `Facts for credit as the spouse or civil partner of a member of the forces`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a Class 3 contribution is credited under regulation 28` `the facts` MEANS
        `the tax year a week falls in` (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`) AT LEAST 1975
    AND `the week falls in a year before 6 April 2016` (`the facts`'s `the first day of the week`)
    AND `the facts`'s `the earnings factors of the member for the year of the week exceed the qualifying earnings factor`
    AND `the conditions for a forces spouse's credit are met` `the facts`
